00:05:13.426 --> 00:05:15.270
QA-- what's the general gist?

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:16.377
What does the company do?

00:05:16.377 --> 00:05:17.210
RUSSELL SMITH: Cool.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.260
So Rainforest QA is a service.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:22.960
So we give you a web interface
and APIs and command line tools

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.740
in order to do your QA.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:27.540
So you can go in and
test in plain English.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:30.850
So whether you're a
developer or a PM,

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:34.150
you can write basically
regression tests

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.634
for your web app.

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.800
Then you can trigger them
either using the interface

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:40.989
or using the API or put
it into your CI build,

00:05:40.989 --> 00:05:43.030
which is one of the most
common ways of doing it.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.320
So we enable you to do
human powered QA super,

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:49.690
super fast in a normal
continuous integration build.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.370
So a lot of our
customers are using

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.930
it to speed up their
release process

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:57.540
by doing their QA in stuff
like CircleCI or Jenkins,

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.590
which is pretty cool.

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:02.260
The other thing is because
it's in plain English,

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.220
it's enabling other
people on the team

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:07.570
to write more maintainable tests
than would be with something

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.850
like general automation tools.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:12.610
Which if you guys
have ever used them,

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:14.590
are generally pretty brittle.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:18.340
Writing stuff in plain English,
whilst it has its nuances,

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:21.660
generally leads to a test that
is more reliable once you've

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:22.782
got it nailed down.

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:24.490
MARK MANDEL: So I can
write like a script

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:26.960
where I could be like, go
get a product that's green,

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:28.605
and then put it in
your shopping cart

00:06:28.605 --> 00:06:29.980
and then go through
